  // jakx-only, evidence is the field table
  // engine-quick-tier-6: tried extending this same class to ops 55, 66 and
  // 110 (the identical raw188/raw192/raw12 shape as the two sites above), and
  // each fix only unmasked the next one (op 55 -> op 66 -> op 111 -> op 138),
  // with at least four more independent sites past that point (ops 156 via
  // raw184, 270 and 280 via a1/v1, 378 via v1, each its own register and each
  // needing its own point cast). This function evidently repeats the same
  // per-prim-type debug print block (sphere/mesh/group) several times over
  // with the compiler re-deriving the process-drawable chain fresh each time
  // rather than caching it, so the cast count keeps growing with no end in
