  // explicit (pointer float) cast at every read and write site; op 476
  // (offset 16) is the first to fail on its own, the rest cascade the same
  // way. a2 at op 475 (the vadd.xyz result store back into v1-108 offset
  // 16, sqc2) resolves to a bare pointer on its own and fails to compile
  // ("No method or function named s.vf! for type pointer"); its sibling
  // a0-58 at the same offset auto-resolves for the .lvf read but the s.vf!
  // write needs the same explicit (pointer int128) cast the water-anim
  // rung already established for this class (see the cam-vehicle entries
  // below). The v1-110 block's own vadd store (a2 at op 530, same shape,
  // offset 0 rather than 16) needs the identical cast; unlike v1-110's
  // scalar-float reads, casting a2 alone here does not disturb the
  // pointer-arithmetic base.
  // A second, near-identical block starting at op 515 (v1-110, the
  // 'interp lookup) repeats the same shape but its own vector-add target is
  // offset 0 rather than offset 16 (a2/a0 computed as v1-110 plus zero, not
  // plus sixteen); casting v1-110 to (pointer float) at any of its scalar
  // read/write sites, tried at offsets 16/20/24 alone and at all six
