  "update-stuff": [
    [[26, 34], "v1", "process-drawable"],
    [[28, 70], "gp", "process-drawable"]
  ],
  // etie-ints/etie-floats (debug segment VU1 register dumps, gated by
  // *debug-segment*): gp is set once per function to a raw VU1 data-memory
  // address (0x1100c000 base, matching the PS2 VU1 data-memory mapping; see
  // etie-init-consts/etie-init-engine for the same base class), then indexed
  // per debug-segment register slot (16-byte stride, matching the VU1
  // register file's own vi/vf layout) and dereferenced with l.wu. The
  // decompiler leaves the indexed address typed plain int (raw address
  // arithmetic, not a real pointer), so every load off it fails ("Could not
  // figure out load"). etie-ints reads one raw uint32 slot twice (once into
