  // "process" sub-field (handle's declared layout: process (pointer
  // process) at offset 0 size 32, pid at offset 32), and op 2
  // dereferences that pointer-to-pointer once more. This is exactly
  // jak3's own (-> self hand process 0) idiom
  // (goal_src/jak3/engine/camera/pov-camera.gc:315-316, the identical
  // "when (not s2-0) ... othercam parent invalid" guard), not a raw
  // handle value: casting v1 to "handle" at op 1-2 (tried first, see
  // git history) left op 2 unresolved because handle is a 64-bit value
  // type, not something an l.wu can dereference; (pointer process) is
  // the type that actually matches what l.wu addresses. Cast at the
  // failing read op (2), not the defining sllv at op 1. Every sllv site
  // in this file stays flagged "Unsupported inline assembly instruction
  // kind" regardless (the self-referential sllv v1, v1, r0 shape does
  // not fold, matching update-eyes/dirty-eyes' own documented
  // conclusion above); only the field-typing half is fixed here.
  // s3 (op 2's own result, the live process pointer) then reads
  // process-drawable's own root/node-list/draw/skel fields (raw
  // 184/188/188/192/196, declared 188/192/192/196/200 per the +4
  // trap) at ops 14/18/24/38/47/64, matching jak3's own repeated
  // (the-as process-drawable s2-0) at every one of these accesses
  // (goal_src/jak3/engine/camera/pov-camera.gc:315-336). s3 is reused
  // for something unrelated starting op 145 (a completely different
  // definition further down in the same function), so the cast is
  // scoped to this variable's own live range, not the whole function.
  // A second, independent (-> self hand process 0) occurrence near the
  // end of :code (op 114-116), matching jak3's own second use
  // (goal_src/jak3/engine/camera/pov-camera.gc:381, "(let ((a0-27
  // (-> self hand process 0))) (when (or (-> self die?) ...
  // (ja-anim-done? a0-27)))"); the result only needs a plain process
  // read here (ja-anim-done? takes a process), no further
  // process-drawable cast.
